 "result": "Call order at the end of a request:\n\n1. `Tessel.finalize_request` (`src/tessel/app.py:1021`) turns the view's return value into a response with `make_response` (`app.py:1224`). It then calls `finalize_reply`.\n2. `Tessel.finalize_reply` (`src/tessel/app.py:1394`) runs the post-processing. At line 1416 it calls `self.session_interface.persist_session(self, ctx._get_session(), response)`.\n3. `SignedCookieSessionInterface.persist_session` (`src/tessel/sessions.py:337`) does the writing:\n   - It reads the cookie settings through the `get_cookie_*` helpers.\n   - If the session was accessed, it adds `Vary: Cookie`.\n   - If the session is empty and modified, it calls `response.delete_cookie` and returns.\n   - If the session is empty and not modified, it returns without touching the cookie.\n   - Otherwise it checks `cookie_needs_write` and computes the expiry with `get_expiration_time`.\n   - It signs the data with `make_signer(app).dumps(dict(session))`.\n   - It then calls `response.set_cookie(...)` (line 374).\n\n`SessionInterface.persist_session` (`sessions.py:263`) is the abstract base method. I didn't read `finalize_reply` beyond line 1416, so there may be other steps in it that I haven't checked.\n\nThe test client also calls `persist_session` directly, at `src/tessel/testing.py:177`.",
